<title>USA: NY state governor sets Swiss bank news conference.</title>
<headline>NY state governor sets Swiss bank news conference.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York State Gov George Pataki said on Wednesday that he planned to hold a news conference on Thursday with the state banking superintendent about &quot;New York State, Swiss banks and the Holocaust.&quot;</p>
<p>A spokesman for Pataki declined to say any more about the purpose of the news conference, which was disclosed in a prepared statement, and which will be held in New York City at 1400 EST.</p>
<p>Pataki's spokesmen had said the governor was studying proposals to curb the activities of Swiss banks to pressure them to reach a settlement with the victims of the Holocaust.</p>
</text>
